(A) now, so integrate-engine and integrate-load can drop v1 `vfs::Vfs` (a path<->FileId table) from blaze-engine and blaze-cargo/src/tree.rs: add to `Db` in crates/base-db/src/db.rs, next to `resolve_path` (line ~316):

    /// The file a source root names at `path`, tracked as `resolve_path`'s lookup outside the anchor's root is.
    pub fn file_for_path(&self, path: &VfsPath) -> Option<FileId> {
        let file = crate::named::lookup(self, path)?;
        let there = self.source_root(self.file_source_root(file).source_root_id(self));
        (there.source_root_ref(self).file_for_path(path) == Some(&file)).then_some(file)
    }
    /// The path the file's source root has it at.
    pub fn path_for_file(&self, file: FileId) -> Option<&VfsPath> {
        let root = self.source_root(self.file_source_root(file).source_root_id(self));
        root.source_root_ref(self).path_for_file(&file)
    }

(B) at the flip (once ide-db and load-cargo are deleted and nothing else uses vfs::Vfs), base-db owns the source-path types itself. Staged already, no `mod` line names them yet: crates/base-db/src/source_path.rs (VfsPath, AnchoredPath, AnchoredPathBuf, same API as vfs's, + tests source_path/tests.rs) and crates/base-db/src/file_set.rs (FileSet, FileSetConfig, FileSetConfigBuilder; FileSetConfig without `fst`: one hash probe per distinct prefix length, same longest-byte-prefix result; `partition` takes (FileId, &VfsPath) pairs; + tests file_set/tests.rs ported from vfs). The flip edits: lib.rs `mod file_set; mod source_path;`, line 62 `pub use vfs::{...}` -> `pub use paths::{AbsPath, AbsPathBuf}; pub use span::FileId; pub use crate::{file_set::{FileSet, FileSetConfig, FileSetConfigBuilder}, source_path::{AnchoredPath, AnchoredPathBuf, VfsPath}};`, line 166 `vfs::FileId` -> `FileId`; each `use vfs::...` line in content.rs:16, change.rs:9, view.rs:28, input.rs:25+1766, files.rs:28, named.rs:28, db.rs:30 (+232/345 `vfs::AbsPath*`), crate_attrs.rs:25, editioned_file_id.rs:10 (+141/151), reparse.rs:389, tests.rs:13, budget_tests.rs:8, files/tests.rs:9, maintain/tests.rs:13, trees/tests.rs:8, tests/memo_properties.rs:7 -> the same names from `crate::`; Cargo.toml `vfs` -> `paths`. integrate-vfs makes the (B) edits itself in one step at the flip (small exact edits, re-reading each file) unless you'd rather; refuse within two check passes if you object to base-db owning these types. (A) too if not taken in two passes.
